  "content": "[Intro]\n[Am7]\nWhen\n\n[Verse 1]\n[Am7]I woke up this morn\nin' Had a\nsmile run across my\n[E7]face. My\n[Am7]baby from town just a\n[Dm]had to get down, Come and\n[E]drag me all over the place.\nGonta\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Am7]drive on a flatbed\ntrailer truck Down on\nhighway fifty nine.\n[E7]\n[Am7]I had the blues and my\n[Dm]baby, she knew She's\n[E]holdin' little piece of mind.\nDown\n\n[Chorus]\n[Dm]brownie,\nMy brownie down\n[Am7]town,\nDown brown\n[B7]ie.\n[E7]\n[B7]  [D7]\n[B7][D7]Got my\n\n[Verse 3]\n[Am7]share and I'm a black hand\ncotton field Just to\ntry and keep myself alive.\n[E7]Eatin'\n[Am7]red beans and rice with the\n[Dm]right sauce, it's nice Or\n[E]anything you wanna try.\n\n[Solo 1]\n[Am7]\n[E7]\n[Am7]\n[Dm]\n[E]\n\n[Solo 2]\n[Dm]\n[Am7]\n[B7]\n[E7]\n[B7]  [D7]\n[B7][D7]Now I'm\n\n[Verse 4]\n[Am7]hitchin' a ride back from\nBrownie's, I'm kind of\nsad but I feel alright.\n[E7]The\n[Am7]cold night it stings but I\n[Dm]got me some wings, I'll be\n\n[Outro]\n[E]flyin' into Houston to-\nnight. [Am7]",
